5.text:
For the cross

\begin{equation*}
X_{i}=Y_{i}e_{K_{i}},\qquad Y_{i}\sim U(-1,1),\;K_{i}\sim
{\rm Unif}\{1,\dots ,d\},
\end{equation*}
i.i.d., put $S_{d}=\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\}$.  On the event
$\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{d}{\rm \;distinct}\}$

\begin{equation*}
{\rm Vol}_{d}\!\left({\rm conv}S_{d}\right)=\frac{1}{d!}
\prod_{i=1}^{d}|Y_{i}|,
\qquad
{\mathbb P}\{K_{i}{\rm \;distinct}\}=\frac{d!}{d^{d}},
\end{equation*}
and ${\mathbb E}|Y|=1/2$.  Hence

\begin{equation*}
{\mathbb E}V_{d}=\frac{d!}{d^{d}}\frac{1}{d!}{\mathbb E}|Y|^{d}
       =\Bigl(\frac1{2d}\Bigr)^{d},\qquad {\mathbb E}V_{1}=1/2,
\end{equation*}
the usual $0$–volume being obtained on the collision event.

With $I_{0}={\mathbb E}\sqrt{Y_{1}^{2}+Y_{2}^{2}}$

\begin{equation*}
I_{0}= \int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}\,du\,dv
     =\frac{\sqrt2+{\rm arsinh}1}{3}
     =\frac{\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)}{3}
     \approx0.765196 ,
\end{equation*}
and ${\mathbb E}|Y_{1}-Y_{2}|=2/3$,

\begin{equation*}
E_{d}:={\mathbb E}\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
      =\frac1d\frac23+\frac{d-1}{d}I_{0}
      =\frac{2/3+(d-1)I_{0}}{d},\qquad i\ne j .
\end{equation*}
For the $d+1$ point set

\begin{equation*}
\bar D_{d}
 =\frac{d{\mathbb E}\|X\|+\binom d2E_{d}}{\binom{d+1}{2}}
 =\frac{1+(d-1)E_{d}}{d+1}
 =\frac{\,d+\tfrac23(d-1)+(d-1)^{2}I_{0}\,}{d(d+1)} ,
\qquad\bar D_{1}=1/2 .
\end{equation*}

Hence with the usual $\binom{d+1}{2}$ average

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}:=\frac{{\mathbb E}V_{d}}{\bar D_{d}}
     =\frac{(2d)^{-d}d(d+1)}
            {d+\tfrac23(d-1)+(d-1)^{2}I_{0}}
     =\frac{(d+1)d^{\,1-d}2^{-d}}
            {d+\tfrac23(d-1)+(d-1)^{2}I_{0}},\qquad R_{1}=1,
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}= \frac{(d+1)(2d)^{-d}}{1+(d-1)E_{d}}\;,
\qquad 
E_{d}= \frac{2/3+(d-1)I_{0}}{d}.
\end{equation*}

In particular

* $R_{1}=1.00000$,
* $R_{2}= \dfrac{3/8}{\,2+2/3+I_{0}\,}\approx0.10927$,
* $R_{3}= \dfrac{4/72}{\,3+4/3+4I_{0}\,}\approx7.51\times10^{-3}$,
* $R_{4}\approx3.79\times10^{-4}$,
* $R_{5}\approx1.51\times10^{-5}$,

and $R_{d}=O\!\left((2d)^{-d}\right)$.  The series is therefore
dominated by the first two terms,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}
 =1+0.10927+0.00751+0.00038+0.000015+\cdots
 \approx1.1172,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $S_{\infty}\simeq1.117$ to three figures, $S_{\infty}\approx
1.12$ with the $d=1$ term contributing the unit $1$ and the whole
non-trivial tail $R_{d\ge2}\approx0.117$.  On the $X_{i}-X_{j}$
normalisation ${\mathbb E}\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|$ the same calculation gives
$r_{d}=(2d)^{-d}/E_{d}$ and $\sum_{d\ge1}r_{d}\approx1.094$, the
$1.117$ value being the conventional $\binom{d+1}{2}$ average which
includes the $0\leftrightarrow X_{i}$ pairs.  This is the $1.12$
volume-to-distance constant for the i.i.d. uniform-on-the-cross
model.  The distinct-axis, $d!/d^{d}=1$, variant is
$R_{d}^{\rm det}=2^{-d}(d+1)/\{d![1+(d-1)I_{0}]\}$ with
$\sum_{d}R_{d}^{\rm det}\approx1.250$.

